open NumberField GlobalTheory.FieldSize

/-- **Weber's Theorem on Ray Class Fields of Imaginary Quadratic Fields**.

Let $K$ be an imaginary quadratic number field ($\dim_\mathbb{Q} K = 2$, discriminant $d_K < -4$)
and let $L$ be a lattice with complex multiplication by the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_K$.
For any integer $n \ge 1$, the extension of $K$ generated by the values of the Weber functions
evaluated at the $n$-torsion points of the elliptic curve $\mathbb{C}/L$ is the ray class field of $K$
modulo $n \mathcal{O}_K$.

Reference: [weber1908]. -/
def WeberRayFieldSt : Prop :=
  ∀ (K : Type) [Field K] [NumberField K] [_root_.NumberField.IsTotallyComplex K] [Algebra K ℂ], Module.finrank ℚ K = 2 → discr K < -4 →
    ∀ L : PeriodPair, (∀ z, z ∈ L.lattice ↔ ∃ a : 𝓞 K, algebraMap K ℂ (a : K) = z) → ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n →
      ∃ (_ : NumberField (IntermediateField.adjoin K (weberSet L n)))
        (_ : IsAbelianGalois K (IntermediateField.adjoin K (weberSet L n))),
        IsRay (IntermediateField.adjoin K (weberSet L n)) (Ideal.span {(n : 𝓞 K)})

end GlobalTheory.Published
